\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces LogT-normal distribution parameters ($\mu , \sigma $) control the queries per sequence, queries per logical session, and the probability of switching logical sessions. Refinement parameters define the likelihood (\texttt  {patternProbability}) and bounds (\texttt  {min/maxRefinementLength}) of generating a refinement sequence for a given query. Instantiation relies on a softmax \texttt  {temperature} and a \texttt  {maxLogits} cutoff for similarity-based entity selection.}}{8}{table.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
